NOTES [
	• Passion Fruit Braised Pork Butt
	• Slow-braised pork shoulder with a sweet-tangy passion fruit glaze. Caribbean/Brazilian-inspired.
	• Substitutes for passion fruit jam: guava paste thinned with lime juice, mango chutney with extra vinegar, or apricot jam plus fresh passion fruit pulp. For grilled/smoked pork butt, use the same glaze ingredients (reduced by half) as a mop sauce during the last hour. Leftovers make excellent Cuban-style sandwiches.
]
 
INGREDIENTS [
	• 3.1 pounds boneless pork butt (shoulder)
	• 2 teaspoons kosher salt
	• 1 teaspoons black pepper
	• 1 tablespoons smoked paprika
	• 1 teaspoons ground cumin
	• 1 teaspoons garlic powder
	• 2 tablespoons vegetable oil
	• 1 yellow onion, diced
	• 4 garlic cloves, minced
	• 1 tablespoons fresh ginger, grated
	• 1 cups chicken stock
	• 6.4 ounces passion fruit jam
	• 3 tablespoons soy sauce
	• 2 tablespoons apple cider vinegar
	• 1 lime, juiced
	• 1 scotch bonnet or habanero, seeded and minced (optional)
	• 3 tablespoons fresh cilantro, chopped (to garnish)
]
 
STEPS [
	1. Season the pork: Pat pork dry. Cut into 5 cm chunks. Rub with 2 teaspoons kosher salt, 1 teaspoons black pepper, 1 tablespoons smoked paprika, 1 teaspoons ground cumin, and 1 teaspoons garlic powder.
	2. Sear: Heat 2 tablespoons vegetable oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high. Sear pork chunks on all sides until browned, about 8 minutes total. Transfer to a plate.
	3. Build the base: Reduce heat to medium. Add 1 yellow onion, diced and cook until softened. Add 4 garlic cloves, minced and 1 tablespoons fresh ginger, grated; cook 1 minute.
	4. Deglaze and assemble: Pour in 1 cups chicken stock and scrape the bottom. Whisk in 6.4 ounces passion fruit jam, 3 tablespoons soy sauce, 2 tablespoons apple cider vinegar, 1 lime, juiced, and 1 scotch bonnet or habanero, seeded and minced (optional). Return pork and any juices.
	5. Braise: Cover, transfer to a 325°F / 165°C oven. Braise until fork-tender, stirring once at the halfway mark.
	6. Reduce the glaze: Transfer pork to a platter. Simmer braising liquid on the stovetop until syrupy. Return pork, toss to coat.
	7. Finish: Garnish with 3 tablespoons fresh cilantro, chopped (to garnish). Serve over rice, with tostones, or in tacos.
]